<!--
  The swap motif of the app icon, on its own: the two arcs that mean "one in, one out".

  Lifted verbatim from app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher.xml — the green arc (#3FCC1D, on top)
  and the red one (#960615, below) — because shared-ui is commonMain and cannot reach a drawable
  that lives in the Android module. Duplicating it as a composeResources drawable is the house
  pattern: ic_launcher.xml itself is already here, byte for byte, next to ic_goal and ic_whistle.

  The launcher's group (scale 0.65, translate 104) is NOT copied. It only places the motif inside
  the 595.28x597.84 canvas of the icon, and being a uniform transform it says nothing about how the
  two arcs sit relative to each other. What matters is that both are symmetric about (297.64,
  298.92) — the centre of the icon's circle — so the frame below is a square of side 458.12 (twice
  the 229.06 that is the furthest either arc reaches from that centre), translated so the motif is
  centred in it. Centred, not merely cropped: anything that spins this mark turns it on its own
  axis instead of swinging it around an off-centre point.

  Both colours are baked in. This is a two-colour mark, not a tintable icon — draw it with Image,
  not Icon. Note the green is the icon's own (#3FCC1D), which is not the theme's SubstitutionGreen.
-->
